.SS CMT_NO_REGISTER_FIX
.IP
.EX
#define CMT_NO_REGISTER_FIX
#include \f[B]\(dqCMT/ATTRIBUTES/REGISTER.H\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Define it before the first CMT header to leave the \f[CR]register\f[R]
keyword and the compiler\(aqs diagnostics exactly as they are.
.PP
\f[CR]REGISTER\f[R] is still defined, so code written with
\f[CR]REGISTER\f[R] keeps compiling in C++17 and later either way.
Code that still says \f[CR]register\f[R] will hit the compiler\(aqs own
error again (Clang) or warning (GCC, MSVC).
